exports[`zwe-install (SHORT) zwe install --help 1`] = `
"zwe install
------------------
Synopsis
    zwe install [parameter [parameter]...]
------------------
Description
    After you extract Zowe convenience build, you can run this command to install
    MVS data sets.
    If you are using SMPE build, you can skip this command since MVS data sets are
    already prepared during SMPE install.
    ## Installation via Shell
    These Zowe YAML configurations showing with sample values are used:
    \`\`\`
    zowe:
      setup:
        dataset:
          prefix: IBMUSER.ZWE
    \`\`\`
    The dataset allocations and copying of members are done in shell script. Only the "prefix" is required:
    * Use \`--dataset-prefix\` parameter
    * Or in yaml configuration as \`zowe.setup.dataset.prefix\`
    * Note: if both parameters are used, \`--dataset-prefix\` overrides the \`--config\` value
    This is the default behavior.
    ## Installation via JCL
    These Zowe YAML configurations showing with sample values are used:
    \`\`\`
    zowe:
      setup:
        jcl:
          enable: true
          header: '123456'
        dataset:
          prefix: IBMUSER.ZWE
    \`\`\`
    Is done by submitting \`ZWEINSTL\` job. To use JCL, following updates are required:
    * \`zowe.setup.jcl.enable=true\`
    * \`zowe.setup.jcl.header\`
    * This customization replaces the template \`{zowe.setup.jcl.header}\` in \`ZWEINSTL\` job:
    \`\`\`
    //ZWEINSTL JOB {zowe.setup.jcl.header}\`
    \`\`\`
    * Default setting is empty string causing no additional JOB fields will be used - if your site or External Security Manager does not require additional fields, you can skip this
    * Otherwise use \`zowe.setup.jcl.header\` to fill with required fields
    * Notes:
      * JCL syntax is not checked by \`zwe install\` command, however empty lines are filtered out
      * If multiple configurations are used, e.g. \`--config 'FILE(zowe.yaml):PARMLIB(ZOWE.PARMS(YAML))'\`, JCL installation is used
    One line, for example accounting information only:
    \`\`\`
    zowe:
      setup:
        jcl:
          header: '123456'
    \`\`\`
    Multiple lines in Literal style (the pipe characters starts the block of the JCL statements):
    \`\`\`
    zowe:
      setup:
        jcl:
          header: |
            123456,
            //     'Zowe User',"
            //      NOTIFY=&SYSUID"
    \`\`\`
    Expected outputs:
    - \`zowe.setup.dataset.prefix\` shows where the datasets will be installed:
      * \`SZWEAUTH\` contains few Zowe load modules (++PROGRAM).
      * \`SZWESAMP\` contains several sample configurations.
      * \`SZWEEXEC\` contains few utilities used by Zowe.
      * \`SZWELOAD\` contains config manager for REXX.
------------------
Global parameters
    --help|-h  (optional)
        Display this help.
    --debug|--verbose|-v  (optional)
        Enable verbose mode.
    --trace|-vv  (optional)
        Enable trace level debug mode.
    --silent|-s  (optional)
        Do not display messages to standard output.
    --log-dir|--log|-l string (optional)
        Write logs to this directory.
    --config|-c string (optional)
        Path to Zowe configuration zowe.yaml file.
    --configmgr  (optional)
        Deprecated. This behavior is always enabled.
------------------
Parameters for command "install"
    --allow-overwrite|--allow-overwritten  (optional)
        Allow overwritten existing MVS data set.
    --dataset-prefix|--ds-prefix string (optional)
        Install Zowe to this dataset prefix.
        If you specify this value, --config is not required.
    --jcl  (optional)
        Generates and submits JCL to drive the install, rather than using USS utilities.
    --dry-run  (optional)
        Generates and prints JCL but does not execute.
------------------
Example(s)
    zwe install -v -c /path/to/zowe.yaml"
`;

exports[`zwe-install (SHORT) zwe install invalid config 1`] = `
"cat: /not/real/config.yml: EDC5129I No such file or directory. (errno2=0x0594003D)
===============================================================================
